  "proof_scope": [
    "The actual two-parameter off-diagonal cross-ratio correspondence becomes affine after the common chart X=1/(1-vx). Its two outer f weights and both transported factors depend on the same original u. Any family of slopes with uniformly bounded sum of |f(t)| per u costs O(p) on the near-critical branch, by the injective partial permutation and counting second norms.",
    "At each finite prime the common bulk zero set of the true complementary face is exactly the union of positive bulk supports of the primal true face, by a small objective perturbation and exact duality. The true primal has a representative positive everywhere on I. The correctly signed dual recession objective is nonpositive, with equality only for rows vanishing on I.",
